.SH "Detailed Description"
.PP 
extras beyond what Node\&.js FileSystem provides 


.PP
\fBNote\fP
.RS 4
\fBAPI Stability: 2 — Evolving\fP\&. This API is implemented and supported, but its contract is still settling\&. Compatibility is preserved where practical; breaking changes are documented in release notes\&. See \fBAPI stability\fP\&.
.RE
.PP
Most functions for file manipulation are provided by Node\&.js though the FileSystem class\&. The PDG \fBFileManager\fP just adds calls to get particular directory paths and to do file searchs\&.

.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
http://nodejs.org/api/fs.html 
.RE
.PP

.SH "Member Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "findClose (\fBFileFindData\fP inFindData)"

.PP
closes a file search operation and cleans up resources stop and cleanup after a file/directory search

.PP
This takes the original object returned from \fBfindFirst()\fP, and cleans up after the search, releasing all resources used by the search\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinFindData\fP the original object returned from \fBfindFirst()\fP, which \fBfindNext()\fP updates in place
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBfindFirst\fP 

.PP
\fBfindNext\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "string[] findDirs (string name)"

.PP
return a sorted list of directories that match the given name This uses the \fBfindFirst()\fP and \fBfindNext()\fP calls to search for any directories that match the name passed in\&. The name can contain wildcard characters (*\&.txt, or f1?\&.dat)\&. If the name includes a path, it must use Unix format (forward slash "/" as path separators)\&. Colon and backslash are both illegal characters\&. The returned array is sorted lexicographically by node name to provide deterministic cross-platform results\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP the directory name to find
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
a lexicographically sorted array of directories that match the name
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBfindFirst\fP 

.PP
\fBfindNext\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "string[] findFiles (string name)"

.PP
return a sorted list of files that match the given name This uses the \fBfindFirst()\fP and \fBfindNext()\fP calls to search for any files that match the name passed in\&. The name can contain wildcard characters (*\&.txt, or f1?\&.dat)\&. If the name includes a path, it must use Unix format (forward slash "/" as path separators)\&. Colon and backslash are both illegal characters\&. The returned array is sorted lexicographically by node name to provide deterministic cross-platform results\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIname\fP the filename to find
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
a lexicographically sorted array of files that match the name
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBfindFirst\fP 

.PP
\fBfindNext\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "\fBFileFindData\fP findFirst (string inFindName)"

.PP
get the first matching file or directory This searches for any files or directories that match the name passed in, and returns the first one it finds\&. The name can contain wildcard characters (*\&.txt, or f1?\&.dat)\&. If the name includes a path, it must use Unix format (forward slash "/" as path separators)\&. Colon and backslash are both illegal characters\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinFindName\fP the directory or file name to find
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
an object with nodeName, isDirectory, and found fields: \fBnodeName\fP is the full path of the found item; \fBisDirectory\fP is true if the node is a directory, false for files; \fBfound\fP is false if no matching item was found\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBfindNext\fP 

.PP
\fBfindClose\fP 
.RE
.PP

.SS "boolean findNext (\fBFileFindData\fP ioFindData)"

.PP
finds the next file matching the search criteria advance a file/directory search and update its search object

.PP
Continue the search using the same object returned by \fBfindFirst()\fP\&. This updates that object's nodeName, isDirectory, and found fields in place\&. When the return value is true, nodeName and isDirectory describe the next matching item\&. When it is false, the search is exhausted and found is false; do not use the other fields as a new result\&. Call \fBfindClose()\fP with this same object to release the search resources\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIioFindData\fP the original object returned by \fBfindFirst()\fP, updated in place 
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
true if another matching item was found, otherwise false
.RE
.PP
\fBSee also\fP
.RS 4
\fBfindFirst\fP 

.PP
\fBfindClose\fP 
.RE
.PP

